      "id": 1,
      "text": "Aredale was founded in 1881, named after the first postmaster’s daughter, and its name echoes the Pennsylvania town of Airville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://nearbylens.com/cities/usa/ia/aredale/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In spring 1890, local dairy farmers pooled resources to build a cheese‑making factory a mile south of town, sparking Aredale’s growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/aredale_iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Aredale Community Church, standing for over a century, has long been a gathering place for residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://nearbylens.com/cities/usa/ia/aredale/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Aredale Historical Society Museum displays exhibits on agriculture, local industry, and notable residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
